## Open peer-poll questions (re-stated from DESIGN.md for argus + vigil)

**Q1 (argus has authorship context)**: snapshot-eligible computation —
caller-passed (chosen above as the simpler path) vs contract-computed
(HatManager loop, gas-expensive). My lean: caller-passed; argus's call
on whether the gas trade is worth the trust simplification.

**Q2 (vigil has fleet-health.js context)**: `isEarlyCloseEligible(id)` as
a public view function vs off-chain compute from existing fields. My
lean: on-chain view; cleaner CLI surface. Vigil's call on whether
per-triage-tick RPC load at scale would matter (3 agents × N proposals
× 96 HBs/day = bounded; should be fine, but vigil knows the rate-limit
landscape).

